////////////////////////////////////Extent Report//////////////////////////////////////////
1. What is Extent Reports in Selenium?
		○ Extent Reports is a logging and reporting library used to generate detailed, interactive HTML reports for Selenium test executions.

2. What are the key features of Extent Reports?
		○ Interactive HTML reports
		○ Logs with screenshots
		○ Test case status (PASS, FAIL, SKIP)
		○ Timestamped logs
		○ Integration with TestNG, JUnit, Cucumber, etc.

3. How do you add Extent Reports to your Maven project?
<dependency>
    <groupId>com.aventstack</groupId>
    <artifactId>extentreports</artifactId>
    <version>5.0.9</version> <!-- Use latest -->
</dependency>

4. How do you create and initialize an Extent Report in Selenium with Java?

//Creates a Spark HTML report at the specified path
String path = "reports/index.html";

//ExtentSparkReporter is used to configure the look and feel of the report (e.g., theme, title, etc.).
ExtentSparkReporter report = new ExtentSparkReporter(path);


//Creates an instance of ExtentReports — the main class used to manage and generate reports.
ExtentReports extent = new ExtentReports();

//Attaches the configured ExtentSparkReporter to the ExtentReports instance.
extent.attachReporter(report);

//This creates a test entry in the report titled "initial demo".
ExtentTest test = extent.createTest("initial demo");

//Writes all logs to the report file. This finalizes the report and must be called at the end of the test execution.
extent.flush();  // Generates the final report

////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

5. How do you create a test entry in the Extent Report?
ExtentTest test = extent.createTest("Login Test");
test.pass("Navigated to login page");

6. How do you flush the report at the end of test execution?
extent.flush();

7. How do you log different test statuses in Extent Report?
test.pass("Test passed");
test.fail("Test failed");
test.skip("Test skipped");

8. How do you attach screenshots in Extent Reports?
test.addScreenCaptureFromPath("screenshots/login_failed.png");

9. How do you integrate Extent Reports with TestNG or JUnit?
		○ Use a TestNG listener (ITestListener) or a base class to initialize and flush Extent Reports in @BeforeSuite and @AfterSuite.

	4. How do you generate a report for each test suite or each test class?
	• Create separate Extent Test instances per test method or class.
	• Store the Extent Test in a ThreadLocal object for parallel execution.

